{
  "introText": "Sixteen free-response problems spanning all four chapters — four per chapter, Basic to Advanced. Try each one, then reveal the worked solution.",
  "items": [
    {
      "number": "L1",
      "question": { "en": "Find \\( \\mathbf{u}+\\mathbf{v} \\) for \\( \\mathbf{u}=(2,-1) \\), \\( \\mathbf{v}=(3,4) \\).", "ar": null },
      "solution": { "en": "<p>Add componentwise: \\( (2+3,\\,-1+4)=(5,3) \\).</p>", "ar": null },
      "difficulty": "Basic"
    },
    {
      "number": "L2",
      "question": { "en": "Find \\( \\lVert\\mathbf{u}\\rVert \\) for \\( \\mathbf{u}=(6,8) \\).", "ar": null },
      "solution": { "en": "\\[ \\lVert\\mathbf{u}\\rVert=\\sqrt{6^2+8^2}=\\sqrt{100}=10. \\]", "ar": null },
      "difficulty": "Basic"
    },
    {
      "number": "L3",
      "question": { "en": "Find \\( \\mathbf{u}\\cdot\\mathbf{v} \\) for \\( \\mathbf{u}=(1,-2,3) \\), \\( \\mathbf{v}=(4,0,-1) \\).", "ar": null },
      "solution": { "en": "\\[ \\mathbf{u}\\cdot\\mathbf{v}=1(4)+(-2)(0)+3(-1)=4+0-3=1. \\]", "ar": null },
      "difficulty": "Basic"
    },
    {
      "number": "L4",
      "question": { "en": "Verify the Cauchy–Schwarz inequality for \\( \\mathbf{u}=(1,0,1) \\), \\( \\mathbf{v}=(0,1,1) \\).", "ar": null },
      "solution": { "en": "<p>\\( \\mathbf{u}\\cdot\\mathbf{v}=0+0+1=1 \\). \\( \\lVert\\mathbf{u}\\rVert=\\lVert\\mathbf{v}\\rVert=\\sqrt2 \\), so \\( \\lVert\\mathbf{u}\\rVert\\lVert\\mathbf{v}\\rVert=2 \\).</p>\\[ |1|\\le2. \\;\\checkmark \\]", "ar": null },
      "difficulty": "Advanced"
    },
    {
      "number": "L5",
      "question": { "en": "Solve \\( x+y=10 \\), \\( x-y=2 \\).", "ar": null },
      "solution": { "en": "<p>Add the equations: \\( 2x=12\\Rightarrow x=6 \\). Then \\( y=10-6=4 \\).</p>\\[ (x,y)=(6,4). \\]", "ar": null },
      "difficulty": "Basic"
    },
    {
      "number": "L6",
      "question": { "en": "How many solutions does \\( 2x+y=4 \\), \\( 4x+2y=8 \\) have?", "ar": null },
      "solution": { "en": "<p>The second equation is exactly \\( 2\\times \\) the first — the same line. Infinitely many solutions.</p>", "ar": null },
      "difficulty": "Basic"
    },
    {
      "number": "L7",
      "question": { "en": "Solve \\( 2x+y=7 \\), \\( x-y=-1 \\).", "ar": null },
      "solution": { "en": "<p>From the second equation, \\( x=y-1 \\). Substitute: \\( 2(y-1)+y=7\\Rightarrow 3y=9\\Rightarrow y=3 \\), so \\( x=2 \\).</p>\\[ (x,y)=(2,3). \\]", "ar": null },
      "difficulty": "Intermediate"
    },
    {
      "number": "L8",
      "question": { "en": "For which value of \\( k \\) is \\( x+3y=2 \\), \\( 2x+6y=k \\) consistent?", "ar": null },
      "solution": { "en": "<p>Row 2's coefficients are exactly \\( 2\\times \\) row 1's, so the right-hand sides must match the same scaling: \\( k=2(2)=4 \\).</p>", "ar": null },
      "difficulty": "Advanced"
    },
    {
      "number": "L9",
      "question": { "en": "Compute \\( A+B \\) for \\( A=\\begin{pmatrix}2&amp;-1\\\\0&amp;3\\end{pmatrix} \\), \\( B=\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;4\\\\-2&amp;5\\end{pmatrix} \\).", "ar": null },
      "solution": { "en": "\\[ A+B=\\begin{pmatrix}3&amp;3\\\\-2&amp;8\\end{pmatrix}. \\]", "ar": null },
      "difficulty": "Basic"
    },
    {
      "number": "L10",
      "question": { "en": "Is \\( A=\\begin{pmatrix}4&amp;2\\\\2&amp;1\\end{pmatrix} \\) invertible?", "ar": null },
      "solution": { "en": "<p>\\( \\det(A)=4(1)-2(2)=4-4=0 \\). Since the determinant is \\( 0 \\), \\( A \\) is not invertible.</p>", "ar": null },
      "difficulty": "Basic"
    },
    {
      "number": "L11",
      "question": { "en": "Compute \\( AB \\) for \\( A=\\begin{pmatrix}2&amp;0\\\\1&amp;3\\end{pmatrix} \\), \\( B=\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;1\\\\0&amp;2\\end{pmatrix} \\).", "ar": null },
      "solution": { "en": "\\[ AB=\\begin{pmatrix}2(1)+0(0)&amp;2(1)+0(2)\\\\1(1)+3(0)&amp;1(1)+3(2)\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}2&amp;2\\\\1&amp;7\\end{pmatrix}. \\]", "ar": null },
      "difficulty": "Intermediate"
    },
    {
      "number": "L12",
      "question": { "en": "Find \\( A^{-1} \\) for \\( A=\\begin{pmatrix}2&amp;3\\\\1&amp;2\\end{pmatrix} \\).", "ar": null },
      "solution": { "en": "<p>\\( \\det(A)=2(2)-3(1)=1 \\), so \\[ A^{-1}=\\begin{pmatrix}2&amp;-3\\\\-1&amp;2\\end{pmatrix}. \\] Check: \\( AA^{-1}=\\begin{pmatrix}4-3&amp;-6+6\\\\2-2&amp;-3+4\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;0\\\\0&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}. \\)</p>", "ar": null },
      "difficulty": "Advanced"
    },
    {
      "number": "L13",
      "question": { "en": "Compute \\( \\det\\begin{pmatrix}3&amp;2\\\\5&amp;4\\end{pmatrix} \\).", "ar": null },
      "solution": { "en": "\\[ 3(4)-2(5)=12-10=2. \\]", "ar": null },
      "difficulty": "Basic"
    },
    {
      "number": "L14",
      "question": { "en": "Compute \\( \\det\\begin{pmatrix}2&amp;3\\\\2&amp;3\\end{pmatrix} \\), and explain why the result makes sense.", "ar": null },
      "solution": { "en": "<p>\\( \\det=2(3)-3(2)=0 \\). The two rows are identical, so this matrix sends some nonzero vector to \\( \\mathbf{0} \\) — exactly the singular case from Theorem 4.2.</p>", "ar": null },
      "difficulty": "Basic"
    },
    {
      "number": "L15",
      "question": { "en": "Compute \\( \\det\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;2&amp;0\\\\3&amp;1&amp;1\\\\0&amp;2&amp;1\\end{pmatrix} \\).", "ar": null },
      "solution": { "en": "<p>Expand along row 1: \\[ 1\\begin{vmatrix}1&amp;1\\\\2&amp;1\\end{vmatrix}-2\\begin{vmatrix}3&amp;1\\\\0&amp;1\\end{vmatrix}+0=1(1-2)-2(3-0)+0=-1-6=-7. \\]</p>", "ar": null },
      "difficulty": "Intermediate"
    },
    {
      "number": "L16",
      "question": { "en": "Given \\( \\det(A)=5 \\) and \\( \\det(B)=-3 \\), find \\( \\det(AB) \\).", "ar": null },
      "solution": { "en": "<p>By Theorem 4.1, \\( \\det(AB)=\\det(A)\\det(B)=5(-3)=-15 \\).</p>", "ar": null },
      "difficulty": "Advanced"
    }
  ]
}
